                <pb facs="0580" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2572: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Emmet</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">The
                                Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-12T13:00:00+01:19">August 12, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 13—6:33 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. The Netherlands Government’s reply to French <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >démarche</hi> in respect to non-intervention in the Spanish conflict gives
                    assurances that pending the conclusion of a collective agreement it will not
                    give permission, within the frame of existing Dutch law, for the export or
                    transit of arms and ammunition to Spain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Emmet</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
